    difficulty: "KOLAY",
    passageText: "Astronomers have confirmed the existence of more than five thousand planets orbiting stars beyond our solar system, the vast majority detected using a technique known as the transit method. This approach relies on measuring the brightness of a distant star over time and watching for a small, regular dip in that brightness, which occurs when a planet passes directly between the star and an observing telescope, briefly blocking a tiny fraction of the star's light. The amount of light blocked reveals the planet's approximate size relative to its star, while the interval between dips reveals its orbital period. The method has a significant limitation: it only detects planets whose orbits happen to be aligned edge-on from Earth's perspective, meaning many more exoplanets almost certainly exist that transit detection simply cannot see. To confirm that a dip in brightness is genuinely caused by a planet rather than another star or instrument error, astronomers typically cross-check transit detections against a second method, such as measuring the star's slight wobble caused by the planet's gravitational pull.",
